# Core workflow

## Language
- Reply to the user in Vietnamese. Keep technical terms in English.
- Code, identifiers, comments, commit messages, and docs are in English.

## What "production" means here
Code a senior can read once and understand. Do enough, no more.
- Readability beats patterns. If a split or abstraction makes the code harder to
  follow, undo it. More files and more functions are not more production.
- Every function, file, and class needs a reason. A helper used once stays inline
  unless its name says something the code does not.
- Related things share a file; unrelated things do not. Three unrelated classes in
  one file is wrong, so is one file per tiny function.
- Never bend production code to make tests easier. Tests adapt to the code.
- Do it the common way real projects do. If unsure what that is, say so; do not invent.
- Names state the role (`reference_data`, `repository`), not the origin or the pattern.
- Handle real risks, not every possible failure. Add logging, retries, health checks,
  or persistence only when the feature needs them; document intentional gaps.
- Build a vertical slice first. Do not build for speculative future requirements.

## Working agreement
- Read `AGENTS.md` and look for an existing pattern before writing a new one.
- Task touching 3+ files, a new module, or an unclear requirement: show a short plan
  or code preview and wait for approval.
- Ask only when the answer changes the design; otherwise pick a default and state it.
- Smallest coherent change. Refactor directly related code when needed; no unrelated cleanup.
- Bug fix: reproduce it with a failing test first, then fix.
- New dependency: justify it in one sentence, add with `uv add`, prefer the stdlib.
- Comment the why, never the what.
- A stop hook runs `make check`. Fix failures at the root cause.
- Final message: what changed, why, how it was verified, follow-ups and risks.

## Never
- Commit, push, or amend unless explicitly asked.
- Read, print, or edit `.env` or any secret. Add new keys to `.env.example` instead.
- Disable a lint rule, add `# type: ignore`, or skip a test to make a check pass without
  telling the user why.
